r's number">e</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-const btn-const-i" data-op=const:i aria-label="imaginary unit i">i</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-cmp btn-cmp-leq" data-op=cmp:leq aria-label="less than or equal to">≤</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-cmp btn-cmp-geq" data-op=cmp:geq aria-label="greater than or equal to">≥</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-cmp btn-cmp-neq" data-op=cmp:neq aria-label="not equal to">≠</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-square" aria-label="raise to the power"><img src="/images/keypad-sqrt.svg?v=18beca97403a" width=27 height=24 alt=""></div><div class="button btn-dark btn-root" aria-label="square root"><img src="/images/keypad-root.svg?v=671786d38371" width=31 height=24 alt=""></div><div class="button btn-dark btn-abs" aria-label="absolute value">|abs|</div><div class="button decimal-separator" aria-label=comma>,</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-semicolon" data-op=op:semicolon aria-label=semicolon>;</div><div class="button btn-dark btn-bracket" aria-label=parentheses>( )</div><div class=button aria-label="letter x">x</div><div class=button aria-label="letter y">y</div><div class="button btn-dark" aria-label=equals>=</div></div></div></template></div></div></div><div class="solver-type solver-title main-content"><h1>Solution - Long multiplication</h1></div><script>(function(){if(typeof window==='undefined'||typeof window.gtag!=='function'){return;}
try{var nav=window.performance&&typeof window.performance.getEntriesByType==='function'?window.performance.getEntriesByType('navigation')[0]:null;if(nav&&nav.type==='back_forward'){return;}
window.gtag('event','solve_success',{event_category:'solver_funnel',solver_type:"V2-LongMultiplication",locale:"en"});}catch(e){}}());</script><div class=main-content><div class=solution-content><div class="card card-body results-wrapper"><div class=results-found><h2>Solution</h2></div><div id=finalResult></div><div class="d-md-none position-sticky bg-white py-2 mb-2" style=top:64px;z-index:20><div class="see-steps d-flex justify-content-center flex-wrap" style=gap:8px><a class=go-to-step href=#finalResult>Final Result</a> <a class=go-to-step href=#see-steps>Steps</a> <a class=go-to-step href=#termsAndTopics>Terms and topics</a></div></div><div class=result><div class=row><div class=col-12><span class=d-none> </span> <span class="result-final hide-when-no-js color-dimgrey" data-result=391> <span data-tooltip-text="Click to Copy" data-tooltip-text-copied="✔ Copied" class=copy-click data-copy=391 data-copy-readable=391 role=button tabindex=0 aria-label="Click to Copy: 391"><span class=math-scroll dir=ltr><math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>391</mn></mrow></math></span></span> </span><div class=show-when-no-js><span class=result-final-nojs>391</span></div></div></div></div><div class=see-steps><a aria-label="See steps" class=go-to-step href=#see-steps>See steps</a> <a aria-label="Learn more with Tiger" class=go-to-step href=#whyLearnThis>Learn more with Tiger</a> <a aria-label="Try this:" class=go-to-step href=#termsAndTopics>Try this:</a></div><div class="solution-dropdown-wrapper-div d-none"><div class="solver-type solution-dropdown-wrapper"><div class=toggle-solution-dropdown-wrapper><p class=more-solution-title>Other Ways to Solve</p><a href=# class=toggle-solution-dropdown>Long multiplication<span class="controls-link down-icon"></span></a></div></div></div></div><h2 class=step-by-step-title-main id=see-steps>Step-by-step explanation</h2><div class=steps-content><div><div class="solution-step step card card-body first"><h3 class=step-title><span class=step-number>1. </span> <span>Set up the factors by place value</span></h3><div class=step-content><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValuePopulate cellPopulateFromInput'><span></span></td><td class='cellValuePopulate cellPopulateFromInput'><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td class='cellValuePopulate cellPopulateFromInput'><span></span></td><td class='cellValuePopulate cellPopulateFromInput'><span>1</span></td><td><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr></table></div></div></div><div class="solution-step step card card-body"><h3 class=step-title><span class=step-number>2. </span> <span>Multiply each place value</span></h3><div class=step-content><p class="text-unit text-unit-main">Method: partial-products long multiplication. Multiply each digit of the multiplier by the multiplicand, shift each row by its place value, then add the partial products to get the final product.</p><p class=table-text-general>Start with the ones digit (7) of the multiplier 17. Multiply it by each digit of the multiplicand 23, from right to left.</p><p class=table-text>Multiply the ones digit of the multiplier (7) by the digit in the ones place of the multiplicand:<br> 7×3=21</p><p class=table-text-carry>Write 1 in the ones place.</p><p class=table-text-carry>Because the product is greater than 9, carry 2 to the tens place.</p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellCarry'><span>2</span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>2</span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr></table></div><p class=table-text>Multiply the ones digit of the multiplier (7) by the digit in the tens place of the multiplicand, then add the carried value (2):<br> 7×2+2=16</p><p class=table-text-carry>Write 6 in the tens place.</p><p class=table-text-carry>Because the product is greater than 9, carry 1 to the hundreds place.</p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellCarry'><span>1</span></td><td class='cellHighlight cellCarry'><span>2</span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>1</span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply cellPartialResultCompleted'><span>6</span></td><td><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr></table></div><p class=text-partial-product>161 is the first partial product.</p><p class=table-text>Now use the tens digit (1) of the multiplier (17). Multiply it by each digit of the multiplicand (23), from right to left.<br><br> Because 1 is in the tens place, this partial product is shifted 1 place(s) left by writing 1 placeholder zero(s).</p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>1</span></td><td><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>6</span></td><td><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td class='cellHighlight cellResultPlaceholder'><span></span></td><td class='cellHighlight cellResultPlaceholder'><span></span></td><td class=cellValueChange><span>0</span></td></tr></table></div><p class=table-text>Multiply the tens digit of the multiplier (1) by the digit in the ones place of the multiplicand:<br> 1×3=3</p><p class=table-text-carry>Write 3 in the tens place.</p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>2</span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>1</span></td><td><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>6</span></td><td><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>3</span></td><td><span>0</span></td></tr></table></div><p class=table-text>Multiply the tens digit of the multiplier (1) by the digit in the tens place of the multiplicand:<br> 1×2=2</p><p class=table-text-carry>Write 2 in the hundreds place.</p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td class=cellHighlight><span>1</span></td><td><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>6</span></td><td><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply cellPartialResultCompleted'><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td><td><span>0</span></td></tr></table></div><p class=text-partial-product>230 is the second partial product.</p></div></div><div class="solution-step step card card-body"><h3 class=step-title><span class=step-number>3. </span> <span>Add the partial products</span></h3><div class=step-content><p class=table-text>Add the partial products by place value to get the final product. Long addition steps can be seen here: <a href='/en/solution/long-multiplication/161%2B230/'>161+230=391</a></p><div class=table-section><table cellspacing=0 class='content-unit-table V2-LongMultiplication'><tr class=header-row><td class=cell-place-value><span>Place value</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>hundreds</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>tens</span></td><td class=cell-acted-on><span>ones</span></td></tr><tr class='row-borrow row-carry'><td class=cell-carry-title><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>×</span></td><td><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>7</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td><span>1</span></td><td><span>6</span></td><td><span>1</span></td></tr><tr><td class=cell-operator><span>+</span></td><td><span>2</span></td><td><span>3</span></td><td><span>0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span></span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>3</span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>9</span></td><td class='cellValueChange cellMultiply'><span>1</span></td></tr></table></div><p class=text-unit>The product is 391.</p></div></div><div class="solution-step step card card-body"><h3 class=step-title><span class=step-number>4. </span> <span>Check your work</span></h3><div class=step-content><p class="text-unit text-unit-main">Check the product by multiplying the same factors again or by estimating their size.<br> Here, <span class=long-multiplication-calculation>23×17=391</span>.<br> The product has the expected place value, so the multiplication checks.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card-body feedback-card"><p>Was this explanation helpful?</p><div><a class="btn btn-outline" target=_blank href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9YeiZClWUjBzNl6R7cfOPfOa-tfxGIUdbnmWG7hGFWZArBA/viewform?entry.316020262=%7B23%7D*%7B17%7D&amp;entry.797116918=V2-LongMultiplication">Yes</a> <a class="btn btn-outline" target=_blank href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9YeiZClWUjBzNl6R7cfOPfOa-tfxGIUdbnmWG7hGFWZArBA/viewform?entry.316020262=%7B23%7D*%7B17%7D&amp;entry.797116918=V2-LongMultiplication">No</a></div><p>How did we do?</p><a target=_blank href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9YeiZClWUjBzNl6R7cfOPfOa-tfxGIUdbnmWG7hGFWZArBA/viewform?entry.316020262=%7B23%7D*%7B17%7D&amp;entry.797116918=V2-LongMultiplication">Please leave us feedback.</a></div><div><div class="step solutions-why-learn-this card card-body" id=whyLearnThis><h2>Why learn this</h2><details><summary>Learn more with Tiger</summary><div class=step-content>Long multiplication is a reliable way to multiply larger numbers by hand. It breaks one large product into smaller digit products, keeps each place value lined up, and then adds the partial products. The same structure helps with decimals because you can multiply whole-number digits first and place the decimal at the end.</div></details></div></div><div><div class="step solutions-topics card card-body" id=termsAndTopics><h2>Terms and topics</h2><div class=step-content><ul class=solution-topics-list><li><a class=related-topic-link href="/en/terms-and-topics/long-multiplication/">Long multiplication</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div><div class="step solutions-topics card card-body" id=relatedLinks><h2>Related links</h2><div class=step-content><ul class=solution-links-list><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.mathsisfun.com/numbers/multiplication-long.html>Long Multiplication - Math is fun</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.khanacademy.org/math/arithmetic-home/multiply-divide/multi-digit-mult/v/multiplication-6-multiple-digit-numbers>Multiplying multi-digit numbers - Khan academy</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.khanacademy.org/math/algebra-basics/basic-alg-foundations/alg-basics-operations-with-decimals/v/multiplying-decimals>Multiplying decimals - Khan academy</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.math-salamanders.com/multi-digit-multiplication.html>Multi-Digit Multiplication Worksheets | Math Salamanders</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://whiteroseeducation.com/latest-news/long-multiplication-method>How to Teach the Long Multiplication Method | White Rose Education</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.mathnasium.com/blog/long-multiplication>How to Do Long Multiplication | Mathnasium</a></li><li><a target=_blank rel=noopener class="related-topic-link underline-text" href=https://www.k5learning.com/free-math-worksheets/fourth-grade-4/multiply-in-columns>Multiply in Columns Worksheets | K5 Learning</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-12 col-lg-4 side-column main-content"><div class="row main-content latest-related"><div class=col-12><div class="latest-list card card-body"><h2>Latest Related Drills Solved</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/84%2A3.5/" aria-label=84*3.5> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>84</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>3.5</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/82%2A87/" aria-label=82*87> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>82</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>87</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/1.124%2A100000000/" aria-label=1.124*100000000> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>1.124</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>100000000</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/472%2A18/" aria-label=472*18> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>472</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/6.838%2A10000000/" aria-label=6.838*10000000> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>6.838</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>10000000</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/18.9%2A3.1/" aria-label=18.9*3.1> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>18.9</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>3.1</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/4.6224%2A10000000/" aria-label=4.6224*10000000> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>4.6224</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>10000000</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/925%2A96/" aria-label=925*96> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>925</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li><li><a href="/en/solution/long-multiplication/1440%2A139/" aria-label=1440*139> <math display=block class=is-hovered><mrow><mn>1440</mn><mo>&sdot;</mo><mn>139</mn></mrow></math> </a> <span class=disclosure-icon></span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></main><script defer src="/js/jquery.min.js?v=87d441de491c"></script><script defer src=/js/site.main1b029e0e7f95744d9c2e.js></script><footer id=footer-content class="container-fluid footer-bottom main-content"><div class=row><div class="col-12 col-lg-2 back back-to-top"><a href=#> <svg xmlns=http://www.w3.org/2000/svg width=24 height=24 fill=none id=backToTopBtn><path fill=#333 fill-rule=evenodd d="M20 11H7.8l5.6-5.6L12 4l-8 8 8 8 1.4-1.4L7.8 13H20v-2Z" clip-rule=evenodd /></svg> Back to top </a></div><div class="col-12 col-lg-10"><ul class=links><li class=footer-link><a href=/privacy-policy>Privacy policy</a></li><li class=footer-link><a href=/legal#tos>Terms of service</a></li><li class=footer-link><a href=/legal#imprint>Impressum</a></li><li class=footer-link><a href=mailto:support@tigermilk.education>Contact</a></li><li class=footer-copyright><p class=copyright>Copyright &#x24B8; 2013-2026<br>tiger-algebra.com</p></li><li class=footer-social><a aria-label="Tiger Algebra - Youtube" rel=noopener target=_blank href=https://www.youtube.com/c/Tiger-algebra><span class=yt-icon></span></a></li></ul></div></div></footer></body></html>